nts [29, 30]. The lower detection rate of conventional radiographs might be attributed to the fact that a PL becomes discernible only when a 30-50% loss of bony mineral content has occurred [23]. Consequently, we", "width": 1654, "height": 2205, "blocks": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Zargar et al. BMC Oral Health", "bbox": {"x": 150.7, "y": 96.0, "width": 275.7, "height": 29.0}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "(2024) 24:28", "bbox": {"x": 483.9, "y": 92.4, "width": 125.20000000000005, "height": 29.900000000000006}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Page 6 of 11", "bbox": {"x": 1371.8, "y": 89.4, "width": 128.4000000000001, "height": 39.20000000000002}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Table 2 The association between tooth type and two dependent variables Tooth type", "bbox": {"x": 153.4, "y": 239.9, "width": 753.8, "height": 66.4}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PL status", "bbox": {"x": 618.6, "y": 275.6, "width": 96.20000000000005, "height": 22.399999999999977}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Mean PL volume (mm3)", "bbox": {"x": 1211.7, "y": 272.4, "width": 169.9000000000001, "height": 54.50000000000006}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Present, n (%)", "bbox": {"x": 618.5, "y": 336.0, "width": 125.20000000000005, "height": 26.69999999999999}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Absent, n (%)", "bbox": {"x": 823.8, "y": 332.8, "width": 125.0, "height": 29.30000000000001}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "0.021*", "bbox": {"x": 1028.9, "y": 333.3, "width": 67.29999999999995, "height": 28.80000000000001}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "0.006*", "bbox": {"x": 1416.8, "y": 330.1, "width": 64.09999999999991, "height": 32.0}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Maxillary first molar", "bbox": {"x": 153.9, "y": 368.6, "width": 182.70000000000002, "height": 29.30000000000001}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "74（61.1%）", "bbox": {"x": 618.6, "y": 368.6, "width": 99.39999999999998, "height": 25.600000000000023}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "47（38.9%）", "bbox": {"x": 827.0, "y": 368.6, "width": 96.20000000000005, "height": 25.600000000000023